&lt;p&gt; The only accepted and scientifically valid medical use of histamine is diagnostic, including tests to assess:&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt; 
&lt;li&gt; The ability of the stomach to secrete acid;&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; The integrity of peripheral sensory nerves (e.g., in leprosy);&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; The circulatory competency in limb extremities; and&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; The presence of a pheochromocytoma.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
